{"id":"word:hebrew:H1270","type":"word","title":"בַּרְזֶל","subtitle":"H1270 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"iron (as cutting); by extension, an iron implement","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בַּרְזֶל (H1270) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 76 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בַּרְזֶל (barzel) means iron (as cutting); by extension, an iron implement First listed occurrence: 1Chr 20 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בַּרְזֶל","transliteration":"barzel","pronunciation":"bar-zel'","strong":"H1270","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1270","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["בַּרְזֶל֙","בַּרְזֶ֑ל","הַ/בַּרְזֶל֙","בַּרְזֶ֔ל","בַּרְזֶֽל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",44],["HTd/Ncmsa",14],["HC/Ncmsa",8],["HRd/Ncmsa",4],["HC/Rd/Ncmsa",3],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",1],["HC/R/Ncmsa",1],["HR/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"iron (as cutting); by extension, an iron implement","usage":"(ax) head, iron.","full":"H1270. barzel בַּרְזֶל noun masculine Deut 19:5 iron (with ל afform.; from piercing ? Late Hebrew id. , Aramaic id. , מַּדְזֶל , , Phoenician ברזל , Assyrian parzillu COT Gloss , (Arabic fetter is loan-word)) — always absolute ׳ב Gen 4:22 74t. ( בַּרְזֶל֑ 4:22 etc.); — 1 iron , literally: a. iron-ore, stone containing iron , Deut 8:9 ; Job 28:2 ; b. as raw material (to be worked) Gen 4:22 ; 1Chr 22:3 , 14 , 16 ; 29:2 (twice in verse); 29:7 ; 2Chr 2:6 ; 2:13 ; 24:12 ; Isa 44:12 ; c. as article of commerce Ezek 27:12 , 19 ; d. as material of furniture , utensils, implements, etc., ב ׳עֶרֶשׂ Deut 3:11 , ב ׳רֶכֶב Josh 17:16 , 18 ; Judg 1:19 ; 4:3 , 13 , ב ׳כְּלֵי Josh 6:19 , 24 compare 1Kin 6:7 ; Num 35:16 , ׳עֵטבֿ Job 19:24 & figurative Jer 17:1 , הַבּ ׳חֲרִצֵי 2Sam 12:31 = 1Chr 20:3 , הַבּ ׳מַגְזְרוֺת 2Sam 12:31 cutting instrument of iron , see Amos 1:3 , ב ׳כַּבְלֵי Psa 149:8 (|| זִקִּיִם ), ב ׳נֵשֶׁק Job 20:24 , ב ׳קַרְנֵי 1Kin 22:11 2Chr 18:10 , ב ׳קִיר & ב ׳מַחֲבַת Ezek 4:3 ; ב ׳בְּרִיחֵי , i.e. of Babylon, ag. Cyrus Isa 45:2 ; compare 1Sam 17:7 & Isa 60:17 (twice in verse) (figurative) 2 tool of iron Deut 27:5 ; Josh 8:31 ; Prov 27:17 (twice in verse); Eccl 10:10 ; Isa 10:34 (metaphor); head of an axe Deut 19:5 ; 2Kin 6:5-6 , so weapon 2Sam 23:7 ; Job 41:19 ; compare also Num 31:22 ; Josh 22:8 where iron as spoil of war. 3 iron in figure of unwatered earth Deut 28:23 ; of Egyptian bondage, הַבּ ׳כּוּר 4:20 ; 1Kin 8:51 ; Jer 11:4 ; of oppression ב ׳עֹל Deut 28:48 ; Jer 28:14 compare 28:13 ; of strength 15:12 (twice in verse); compare ׳ב מִנְעָלֶיךָ Deut 33:25 & Micah 4:13 ב ׳קֶרֶן ; of prophet, firm through Yahweh's might, ׳ב עַמּוּד Jer 1:18 ; of distress, ב ׳בְּרִיחֵי Psa 107:16 compare 107:10 of judgments of ׳י , & 105:18 ; ב ׳שֵׁבֶט 2:9 ; of evil-doers, Jer 6:28 ; Ezek 22:18 , 20 ; simile of scorching sky Lev 26:19 ; ב ׳מְטִיל of bones of hippopotamus Job 40:18 ; ב ׳גִּיד of obstinate neck of Israel Isa 48:4 .","rootNote":"perhaps from the root of 1269 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 20 3","keyReferences":["1Chr 20 3","1Chr 22 3","1Chr 22 14","1Chr 22 16","1Chr 29 2","1Chr 29 2","1Chr 29 7","1Kgs 6 7"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":76,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 20 3","book":"1Chr","chapter":20,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/בַּרְזֶל֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 3","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בַרְזֶ֣ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/לַ/בַּרְזֶל֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Rd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/לַ/בַּרְזֶ֖ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Rd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 2","book":"1Chr","c